.TH CMP 1
.SH NAME
cmp \- compare two files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cmp
[
.B \-s
]
.I file1 file2
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Cmp
compares the two files byte by byte and prints
a message on standard error if the contents differ.
The message gives the position of the first differing byte,
counted from 1, and the line it is on.
When one file is a prefix of the other, the message names the shorter
file and says
.BR EOF .
.PP
The option
.B \-s
prints nothing for differing files
but sets the exit status.
It is recognised only as the first argument.
.SH SOURCE
.B cmd/cmp/main.odin
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
If a file is inaccessible or missing, the exit status is
.BR "can't open" .
If the files are the same, the exit status is empty (true).
Otherwise
.I cmp
reports the first disagreement, or the end of the shorter file, and the
exit status is
.BR differ .
Unlike Plan 9's
.IR cmp ,
a file that is a prefix of the other exits
.B differ
and not
.BR EOF .
.SH BUGS
Both files are read whole into memory before they are compared.
There are no offsets and no
.BR \-l .
